%%%%** Section 1.5
\subsection{Example: Pointers and Arrays}
{\bf (Lewis, Section 3.6)}\\
Consider the original IBM-PC
80 col x 40 rows, display buffer \\

<*chn> This is the graphics hardware that generates
the clunky screen that you use to configure
your {\tt BIOS}.

<*>

\begin{tabular}{l|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}
\hline
      & addr & col 1 & &col 2 & &col 3  & \\ \hline
 row 1 &B8000    & ch &cl &ch &cl &...  \\ \hline
 row 2 &B80A0    & ch &cl &... & & \\ \hline
 ...   & &ch & ...& & & \\ \hline
       & &... & & & & \\ \hline
       & & & & & & \\ \hline
       & & & & & & \\ \hline
       & & & & & & \\ \hline
\end{tabular}

<*chn>
\noindent
where ch is a {\tt char} display character, and
cl is a {\tt char} which encodes the color of that
character position.

